# Bot Company — launch video storyboard (approved storyboard)

1920×1080 · 30 fps · ~94 s · Remotion · **dark look** (near-black gradient, bot colours as accents) · **music + bold on-screen text; no voiceover** · on-screen headlines ≤ 7 words. Status: 12 scenes implemented 2026-10-12; the CFO plan scene sits between the receipts and the end card.

Style (from the whatships refs): one idea per scene, word-by-word blur-in headlines, real UI in floating cards with a soft shadow and slow push-in, cursor with click ripples, blur-dissolve transitions (never hard cuts), music carrying the scene changes. Mascots = the app's own bot avatars (gradient shapes with capsule eyes); Neat Bot = the Neatlogs dot-matrix "nl" tile.

| # | Time | Scene (visual) | On-screen text |
|---|------|----------------|----------------|
| 1 | 0–6s | **Mascot lineup** (MausBot style). The camera dollies along the row of bots and each one gets a beat with its own expression: Primary Bot (violet hex) first, then the specialists. The last stop is **Neat Bot**: its dots spring together into the "nl" tile, it blinks, and it holds as the final hero pose. | — |
| 2 | 6–11s | **Title.** "Bot Company" blurs in glyph by glyph, then the subtitle word by word. The bots pop up from the bottom edge, staggered. | **Bot Company** / A company of AI agents that asks before it acts. |
| 3 | 11–19s | **The team.** Primary Bot in the centre; 9 specialists orbit, then connect to it with curved lines (delegation hub). Each label pops: Research · CFO · GitHub · Legal · Sales · … | One assistant. Nine specialists. |
| 4 | 19–27s | **Real work, real UI.** App card (sidebar + chat). A prompt pill types the US-expansion question. "Delegated to Research Bot / CFO Bot" chips tick in. The cost and token meters climb. *(shots 19, 20)* | Real work. Live costs. |
