| 11 | 87–94s | **End card.** The bots line up again (the same pose as scene 1, so it loops). "Try Bot Company" with the Primary Bot tile, then a URL pill github.com/RK-625/nlhack, then "Built for neatHack 2026 · Neatlogs · Entire · cfo.ai". Fade out. | Try Bot Company |

## Honesty guardrails
- No speed claims: the after runs were not faster.
- The before/after numbers are labelled as one task / our runs, not a benchmark.
- The approved answer's text (shots 22–23) is never zoomed in, because it contains a runway miscalculation.
- The CFO plan page (shot 38) cites local Lumen Labs files such as finance/summary.md. Those figures are not live customer accounting.
- The user asked for three scenarios along with the page. They are not shown as saved. Shot 38's model menu shows Main Scenario only. Shot 39 is unused.

## Asset plan
- **Existing screenshots:** docs/demo/evidence/2026-10-12 (17, 19, 20, 21, 16, 01, 08, 10, 11, 12, 18, 36, 37, 38).
- **No new captures** (decided 2026-10-12). Scene 7 is rebuilt as motion graphics from the real role and tool behaviour in code.
- **Mascots:** rebuilt in Remotion from the real avatar shapes and colours (web/src/lib/avatar).
- **Audio:** "The Last Point" by raspberrymusic (Pixabay, 2:05, in video/public/music/; gitignored because the licence forbids redistributing it on its own) (music only, with composition-length fade-in/out). Previously generated Kokoro files are retained but unused.

## Sprint 3 recovery — 2026-10-12 (historical)
- Sprint3 was the 35-second music-only preview of scenes 1–5. The completed `Main` composition now includes scenes 1–11 plus the CFO plan scene (10b) at 94 seconds.
- Pending controls in scene 5 are a faithful motion reconstruction of `web/src/shell/MessageBubble.tsx`, using the token-limit numbers in shot 21. The approved state is the unmodified screenshot. Shot 01 supplies button styling only; its different dollar-cap run is not presented as this run.

## Completed video
- `npm run render` exports the full 1920×1080, 30 fps `Main` composition to `out/launch.mp4`.
- Scene 7 uses illustrative motion graphics and generic users, based on server-enforced ownership and tool access in the application code. It is not a recorded admin session.
- The final music mix uses the existing local track and no voiceover.
- See `FINAL-REVIEW.md` for validation and evidence boundaries.

